('alict_00003', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In a computer after receiving an instruction from the memory and decoding executing the instruction and placing the result back in the memory is', '["As the von Neumann architecture", "As the Fetch Execute Cycle", "As the abstract model of information creation", "As the data life cycle", "As Big Data Management"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "As the Fetch Execute Cycle". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 3, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00004', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In the Fetch-Execute what happens during the "Execute" stage?', '["The instruction is loaded from memory", "The instruction is decoded", "The operands are fetched from memory", "The instruction is executed by the CPU", "The result is stored in memory"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This occurs during the Fetch where the CPU retrieves the instruction from memory using the Program Counter. Wmfoia ,nd Option 2: In the Decode the CPU interprets the fetched instruction to determine the operation to perform', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 4, '2027 Quiz Series'),
