('alict_00009', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following best explains how a laser printer produces high-quality text and images on paper?', '["It sprays tiny droplets of ink directly onto the paper", "It burns characters into paper using heat", "It uses a laser beam to form an image on a then applies toner. th fnrhla", "It presses pre-formed characters through an inked ribbon. th", "It magnetically charges paper to attract toner particles. th"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Laser printers work by using a laser beam to draw an image on a rotating drum. This drum is electrostatically and where the laser it removes the charge. toner (powder ink) sticks to the parts of the drum where the laser hit', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 9, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00010', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the purpose of registers in a CPU?', '["To store frequently accessed data and instructions", "To perform arithmetic and logical operations", "To control the flow of instructions", "To manage input", "To provide non-volatile storage"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct. Registers provide quick access to data and instructions required for ongoing operations. oekg Option 2: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 10, '2027 Quiz Series'),
