('alict_00015', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the primary benefit of using a multi-core processor?', '["Reduced power consumption", "Increased single-thread performance", "Improved multitasking and parallel processing", "Enhanced security features", "Lower cost compared to single-core processors"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Reduced power consumption While some multi-core processors are designed to be the primary purpose of having multiple cores is not necessarily to reduce power consumption', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 15, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00016', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements about motherboard form factors is correct?', '["ATX motherboards are smaller than Micro-ATX boards. ATX ujq mqjre Micro-ATX mqjre", "Mini-ITX boards typically have more PCIe slots than ATX boards Mini-ITX mqjre PCIe mqjre", "Micro-ATX motherboards are designed to fit in smaller cases while maintaining most features of ATX. ATX fndfyda", "All and Mini-ITX boards have identical size and slot layout. Micro-ATX Mini-ITX mqjre tlu slot", "ATX motherboards cannot support high-end CPUs ATX ujq"]'::jsonb, 3, 'ATX motherboards are the largest standard offering the most expansion RAM and features. So Option 1 is wrong-ATX is not than Micro-ATX. ATX ujq mqjre ,nd Mini-ITX boards are very compact and usually have only one PCIe so option 2 is wrong', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 16, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00017', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'About 30% of is but the rest of it can be used to get the information. What could this be?', '["Barcode", "QR code", "Credit card", "NFC card", "CD"]'::jsonb, 2, 'QR codes are a replacement for barcodes. Although 30% of this part is the other part of it can be used to get the information. This is represented in 2D form. QR wfkla fldgi u.ska tys A barcode is a method of representing data in a machine-readable form', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 17, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00018', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What does the term "clock speed" refer to in the context of a CPU?', '["The speed at which the CPU can execute instructions per second. CPU", "The rate at which the CPU sends data to the RAM. CPU tl RAM tlg", "The frequency at which the CPU''s timer ticks. CPU ghsurh", "The speed of the external clock attached to the CPU. CPU", "The number of cores in the CPU. CPU"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This is the correct answer. Clock measured in hertz (Hz), typically gigahertz (GHz) for modern refers to the number of cycles a CPU can execute per second', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 18, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00019', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statement is true about computers developed in the past?', '["Transistors were used to build third generation computers", "Integrated circuits were used in the second generation of computers. fojk", "Assembly language is used to program in third generation computers", "Software industry was started after the second generation. fojk", "Microprocessors are used in third generation of computers"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Transistors were used to build second generation computers. Advantages of using transistors over than vacuum tubes are they are smaller in size and consumed less power. Assembly language was used to program in this generation', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 19, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00020', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements is true regarding serial and parallel ports on the motherboard?', '["Serial ports transmit data one bit at a whereas parallel ports transmit multiple bits simultaneously", "Parallel ports are typically used for connecting while serial ports are used for printers", "Serial ports have a higher data transfer rate compared to parallel ports", "Parallel ports are obsolete and no longer found on modern motherboards", "Serial ports are known as USB ports in modern computers"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The storage device that matches the given statements is 2) Floppy disk. ,nd Capacity limits to 1.44 MB. The standard capacity for a 3.5-inch floppy disk is 1.44 MB. 3.5 The most popular storage device in the early 90s', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 20, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00021', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following answers contain only manual data collection', '["Plotter", "Barcode Touch OMR", "Barcode Touchscreen", "Joystick", "Barcode Mouse"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Manual data collection methods - Mouse - Keyboard - Touchscreen - Joystick Automated data collection methods - MICR - Barcode reader - OMR Output Devices - Plotter', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 21, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00022', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following lists a computer memory hierarchy in the descending order of access speed?', '["Registers \u2192 Cache \u2192 Main memory \u2192 Hard disk \u2192 Magnetic tape", "Cache \u2192 Registers \u2192 Main memory \u2192 Magnetic tape \u2192 Hard disk", "Registers \u2192 Main memory \u2192 Cache \u2192 Hard disk \u2192 Magnetic tape", "Registers \u2192 Cache \u2192 Hard disk \u2192 Main memory \u2192 Magnetic tape", "Cache \u2192 Main memory \u2192 Registers \u2192 Hard disk \u2192 Magnetic tape"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The memory hierarchy in a computer is usually arranged based on and • Registers → fastest (tiny storage inside the nanosecond access time). • Cache → next fastest (very close to also but slower than registers)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 22, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00023', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following factors most significantly impacts the speed of data reading and writing in Hard Disk Drives', '["The color of the HDD casing. HDD", "The RPM (Revolutions Per Minute) of the HDD. HDD RPM", "The type of operating system used with the HDD. HDD", "The presence of an SSD cache in the HDD. HDD SSD jdrlhla", "The brand of the HDD manufacturer. HDD ksIamdolhdf.a kduh'' Information and Communication ;dlaIKh 2025"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "The RPM (Revolutions Per Minute) of the HDD. HDD RPM". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 23, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00024', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements about the IDE and SATA connectors on a motherboard is false?', '["IDE is serial and SATA is parallel. IDE", "Newer motherboards only feature SATA connectors. kj ujqmqjre SATA", "IDE consumes more power while SA TA consumes less power. IDE", "IDE connectors have lower data transfer speeds while SA TA connectors have higher data transfer speeds. IDE", "IDE is more prone interference in transmission while SATA is less prone interference in transmission. IDE u.ska"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "IDE is serial and SATA is parallel. IDE". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 24, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00025', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'A user upgrades their CPU but finds their computer fails to boot. What is the most likely reason for this issue?', '["The motherboard does not support the GPU. ujq mqjrej GPU", "The RAM is incompatible with the new CPU. RAM kj CPU", "The BIOS needs an update to support the new CPU. kj CPU", "The CPU was not shut down properly previously. CPU fmr ksishdldrj jid", "The power supply unit (PSU) does not match the motherboard''s brand"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Irrelevant in this scenario as the issue concerns the not the GPU. m%Yakh Option 2: since RAM compatibility is more about the motherboard rather than the CPU. RAM Option 3: Many motherboards require a BIOS update to recognize newer CPUs', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 25, '2027 Quiz Series'),
