('alict_00028', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is a type in which data can only be written once and cannot be erased?', '["PROM", "EPROM", "EEPROM", "RAM", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The type of memory where data can only be written once and cannot be erased is PROM (Programmable Read-Only Memory). PROM allows data to be programmed into it a single and once the data becomes permanent and cannot be modified or deleted', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 28, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00029', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'A company is using a printer to create large architectural plans. Which printer type would provide the best results for large-format printing?', '["Inkjet Printer", "Laser Printer", "Plotter", "Dot Matrix Printer", "Thermal Printer"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: While capable of high -quality inkjet printers are generally not optimized for large -format or detailed line drawings required in architectural plans', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 29, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00030', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is a characteristic of direct data entry methods as compared to keyboard entry?', '["Less speed", "Less efficiency", "High reliability", "Takes more time", "Fully automatic"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Direct data entry such as barcode scanning or are typically faster than keyboard not slower. Option 2: Direct data entry methods are designed for high reducing errors and time compared to manual keyboard input. Option 3: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 30, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00031', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Why is firmware considered an essential part of hardware?', '["It provides a user-friendly interface for accessing device features. th", "It integrates the hardware with external software applications. th", "It contains the basic instructions that allow the hardware to function", "It is regularly updated by users to improve hardware speed", "It offers direct connectivity between hardware and peripheral devices. th ,nd fohs'' Information and Communication ;dlaIKh 2025"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Firmware is a specialized type of software that is embedded directly into hardware devices. Unlike regular which can be installed and firmware is stored in non -volatile memory and remains in the hardware unless updated', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 31, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00032', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following tools is best suited for reading checks in a banking system?', '["Optical Character Recognition", "Magnetic Ink Character Recognition", "Bar code reader", "Magnetic strip reader", "Optical Mark Recognition"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Magnetic Ink Character Recognition". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 32, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00033', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'During the execution of a machine which of the following correctly describes the typical sequence of actions in the Fetch-Execute considering modern processor optimizations?', '["The instruction is fetched from and results are while the next instruction starts fetching in parallel. Wmfoia", "The instruction is executed followed by and storing results in the registers. Wmfoia", "The processor fetches multiple instructions executes them out of then decodes and stores them in sequence. ilikh Wmfoia lsysmhla ,nd", "Fetching and decoding occur simultaneously for all instructions in a and execution happens only after all instructions are available. jevigykl Wmfoia", "The processor first checks for then fetches and decodes multiple instructions before executing them in a predetermined order. ilikh lr\" miqj Wmfoia lrhs'' Information and Communication ;dlaIKh 2025"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Modern processors use which means they overlap these stages for different instructions. While one instruction is being the next instruction can be and the one after that can be fetched. This parallelism significantly speeds u p processing', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 33, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00034', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of the third generation of computers?', '["Use of integrated circuits", "Smaller size and faster processing speed", "Use of vacuum tubes", "Increased reliability", "Introduction of high-level programming languages"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: True. The third generation of computers made use of integrated circuits (ICs), which were much smaller and more reliable than the vacuum tubes used in the previous generation. Option 2: True', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 34, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00035', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What type of memory can be erased using ultraviolet (UV) light and reprogrammed?', '["PROM", "EPROM", "EEPROM", "RAM", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is EPROM (Erasable Programmable Read-Only Memory). EPROM is a type of non- volatile memory that can retain data even when the power is turned off. Unlike PROM (Programmable Read-Only Memory), which can only be programmed EPROM can b e erased and reprogrammed multiple times', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 35, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00036', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which type of cache memory is typically embedded directly in the processor?', '["Level 1 cache", "Level 2 cache", "Level 3 cache", "External cache", "Virtual cache"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is Level 1 cache (L1). Level 1 cache is a high-speed memory embedded directly within the processor itself. It provides the fastest access to frequently used data and as it is located closest to the CPU cores', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 36, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00037', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'The most suitable type of printer as a portable printer', '["Dot matrix printer", "Laser Printer", "Thermal printer", "Line printer", "Daisy wheel printer"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Thermal printer". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 37, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00038', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Who invented the concept of storing and controlling computer programs?', '["Charles Babbage", "Blaise Pascal", "Joseph Jacquard", "John von Neumann", "Gottfried Wilhelm"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "John von Neumann". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 38, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00039', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following correctly represents the memory hierarchy from fastest to slowest?', '["Cache \u2192 Registers \u2192 RAM \u2192 magnetic tapes", "Registers \u2192 Cache \u2192 RAM \u2192 magnetic tapes", "magnetic tapes \u2192 RAM \u2192 Cache \u2192 Registers", "RAM \u2192 Cache \u2192 Registers \u2192 magnetic tapes RAM\u2192", "Cache \u2192 Registers \u2192 magnetic tapes \u2192 RAM"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Memory hierarchy refers to the structure and organization of different types of memory in a computer arranged in levels based on and cost. Registers are the fastest memory in the computer', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 39, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00040', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following was not a significant contribution to the development of computing in the 20th century?', '["The creation of the ENIAC computer", "The development of the transistor", "The invention of the telegraph", "The development of the personal computer", "The creation of the World Wide Web"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This was a groundbreaking development in the marking the advent of electronic computing. Option 2: Invented in 1947, transistors revolutionized computing by replacing bulky vacuum tubes and enabling and more reliable computers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 40, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00041', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is the advantage of direct entry input devices over keyboard?', '["Higher processing speed", "No need for user interaction", "Reduced input time and more intuitive interface wvq", "Reduced space for device setup", "Cost-efficiency in bulk production"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Direct entry input such as barcode and have several advantages over traditional keyboards', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 41, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00042', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following best describes the stored program concept?', '["Instructions are manually entered during program execution", "Instructions and data share the same memory", "The program must be stored in ROM to execute", "Each instruction is stored in separate external hardware. Wmfoilau fjku lr", "Programs are stored permanently on the processor"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is not accurate. In the stored program instructions are preloaded into memory and fetched automatically by the processor during execution. ilikh iajhxl%Shj ,nd', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 42, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00043', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is a key difference between a laser printer and an inkjet printer?', '["A laser printer uses liquid while an inkjet printer uses toner powder", "An inkjet printer is typically faster and produces higher-quality prints than a laser printer", "A laser printer uses toner powder and is more cost -effective for high-volume printing than an inkjet printer", "Inkjet printers are more suitable for printing high volumes of while laser printers are best for images", "A laser printer requires more maintenance than an inkjet printer due to frequent ink cartridge replacements"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "A laser printer uses toner powder and is more cost -effective for high-volume printing than an inkjet printer". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 43, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00044', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What does the PET scanner stand for?', '["Personal Energy Transfer scanner", "Positron Emission Tomography scanner", "Portable Electronic Test scanner", "Proton Electron Transmission scanner", "Pre-Emptive Technical Examination scanner"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Positron Emission Tomography scanner". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 44, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00045', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the function of cache memory in a computer system?', '["To store permanent data for long-term use", "To improve the speed of accessing frequently used data", "To act as an interface for external devices", "To backup data in case of a system crash", "To replace main memory during operations"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Permanent data storage is a function of storage devices like or not cache memory. Cache memory is temporary and volatile. Option 2: Correct. This is the primary function of cache memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 45, '2027 Quiz Series'),
