('alict_00048', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which component of Von Neumann Architecture is responsible for executing instructions?', '["Memory", "Input unit", "Arithmetic Logic Unit", "Control Unit", "Output unit"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Memory The memory component stores data and instructions. It holds both the program instructions and the data needed for execution but does not execute instructions itself', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 48, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00049', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not a feature of Cache memory?', '["Larger in size compared to the main memory. m%Odk", "Acts as a moderator between the CPU and RAM. CPU RAM", "Provides high speed data access to the processor. ilikhg", "Stores frequently used Computer programs and applications", "Cache memory is typically made up of SRAM"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Cache memory is designed for not capacity. It is typically made up of Static Random-Access Memory (SRAM). It is a high-speed memory located close to the CPU to store frequently accessed data. The small size helps maintain its fast access time. th tys', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 49, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00050', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following storage technologies has no moving parts?', '["Hard Disk Drive", "Solid-State Drive", "Magnetic Tape", "Floppy Disk", "DVD Drive"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: HDD (Hard Disk Drive) uses spinning magnetic platters and a moving read HDD Option 2: use flash memory (NAND -based storage) and have no moving making them more and more energy-efficient than traditional drives', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 50, '2027 Quiz Series')
