('alict_00051', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the purpose of an SSD (Solid State Drive) in a computer?', '["To temporarily store data for quick access by the CPU. CPU tl u.ska blauka", "To provide long-term storage with faster read", "To manage the computer''s graphical rendering and display", "To act as a backup power source during outages", "To control the computer''s cooling system and temperature"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) To provide long -term storage with faster read because an SSD (Solid State Drive) is a storage device that uses flash memory to store data offering faster performance than traditional (Hard Disk Drives). ukao SSD', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 51, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00052', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In terms of how is OCR superior to MICR?', '["OCR recognizes a wider range of including handwritten text. OCR", "OCR processes data faster than MICR. OCR MICR g", "OCR supports barcode while MICR does not. OCR", "OCR relies on magnetic while MICR does not. OCR", "OCR is more cost-effective than MICR. OCR MICR g"]'::jsonb, 1, '• OCR (Optical Character Recognition) Can recognize printed and handwritten text in different fonts and making it highly versatile', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 52, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00053', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is false about registers?', '["Registers are limited in capacity", "They are located within computer''s central processing unit", "Registers hold data that are used for current operations of the CPU", "They are slower than L1 cache memory L1 cache", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: True. Registers have very limited usually measured in bits or a few bytes 32 -bit or 64-bit registers). Option 2: True. Registers are part of the used for immediate storage and fast access during processing. Option 3: True', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 53, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00054', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which answer includes a system firmware and an application software respectively?', '["Utility Zoom", "Device data entry GIMP Odjl\"", "GIMP", "Utility computer ADA", "MS SQL Audacity MS SQL Audacity"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "MS SQL Audacity MS SQL Audacity". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 54, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00055', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the answer for devices in descending order as Considering the access speed?', '["Flash L3 Registers", "L1 NVMe Flash RAM L1", "NVMe L3 Hard Flash Magnetic tape NVMe L3", "L2 Hard Memory Magnetic tape L2", "L3 L2 Hard disk"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "L3 L2 Hard disk". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 55, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00056', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is a feature of the fifth-generation computers?', '["Using many transistors", "Use of large-scale integrated circuit technology", "Use of technologies such as artificial intelligence", "Introduction of PDP 11 computers", "Use of keyboard and mouse"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The main feature of fifth generation computers is the use of technologies such as artificial intelligence. miajk The transistor was used in the second generation of computers. g%dkaisiagrh Large scale integrated circuit was used in the fourth generation of computers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 56, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00057', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following ports is commonly found on the back I', '["USB port", "HDMI port", "RJ-45 port", "VGA port", "PS"]'::jsonb, 3, 'USB port USB ports are used for connecting various peripheral devices external drives) but not for network connections. 2) HDMI port HDMI ports are used for video and audio output to displays TVs), not for networking', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 57, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00058', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which technology is commonly used in logistics to track products during shipping by scanning tags attached to the items?', '["QR Code", "NFC", "RFID", "GPS", "Barcode"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "RFID". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 58, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00059', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which type of printer is best suited for printing on unusual surfaces like or metal?', '["Laser Printer", "UV Printer", "Inkjet Printer", "Thermal Printer", "Line Printer"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Laser printers are optimized for paper-based printing and cannot print directly on or metal. They use toner powder for printing. Option 2: Correct. A UV printer is a specialized printing device that uses Ultra Violet (UV) light to instantly dry ink as it is printed', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 59, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00060', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Through which of the decode the instructions according to the fetch execute cycle?', '["Arithmetic Logical Unit", "Control Unit", "Cache Memory", "Main Memory", "Accumulator"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Arithmetic Logical Unit executes arithmetic and logical operations. wxl Option 2: Control Unit (CU) is responsible for decoding instructions during the Fetch-Execute cycle', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 60, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00061', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not a typical feature of a joystick?', '["Directional movement control", "Buttons for additional functions", "Touchscreen input", "Axis-based motion detection", "Vibration feedback"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Directional movement control Typical feature. Joysticks are primarily used for controlling direction moving a or cursor on screen). 2) Buttons for additional functions Typical feature', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 61, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00062', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which storage method requires internet access to retrieve data?', '["Local storage", "Hard Disk Drive", "Compact Disk", "Cloud storage", "Tape Drive"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Data stored locally on your device) does not require internet access to retrieve. lr Option 2: A hard disk is a physical device on your so no internet access is needed to retrieve data', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 62, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00063', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following best explains how different types of computer memory interact with the CPU during processing?', '["The CPU directly executes all instructions from secondary eliminating the need for RAM and cache memory. RAM", "Cache memory is used to store frequently accessed reducing the time required for the CPU to fetch instructions from RAM", "The Control Unit (CU) manages all data storage while the ALU directly communicates with the hard drive for faster processing", "RAM retains instructions allowing the CPU to execute them without requiring secondary storage access. RAM Wmfoia", "Registers store large amounts of data ensuring the CPU has immediate access to all necessary instructions"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: CPUs cannot directly execute instructions from secondary storage (like hard drives). Secondary storage is too slow. RAM is essential for holding actively used data and instructions. CPU Option 2: This accurately describes the role of cache memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 63, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00064', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'As of February 2025, Intel''s latest processor line is the Core Ultra Series. Which of the following statements is true about Intel''s Core Ultra processors?', '["They continue to use a monolithic design for improved performance", "They are the first Intel processors to feature a chiplet-based architecture. Chiplet", "They lack integrated AI capabilities", "They are compatible with the older LGA 1700 socket. LGA 1700 socket", "They only support DDR5 memory and do not work with DDR4. Tjqka DDR5"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: They do not use a monolithic design. Option 2: Intel''s Core Ultra processors do use a chiplet-based design. Intel Core Ultra ilik chiplet Option 3: They do have integrated AI capabilities via the Neural Processing Unit (NPU)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 64, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00065', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is responsible for specifying address of a Memory location?', '["RAM", "Control Bus", "Hard Disk", "Address Bus nih", "Data Bus"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: RAM is a volatile memory in a computer system that temporarily stores data and instructions actively used by the CPU', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 65, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00066', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the name of the type of processors in which pins are located on the processor?', '["LGA", "PGA", "BGA", "MGA", "SGA"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: In LGA (Land Grid Array) the pins are located on the socket of the not on the processor. The processor has flat contact points that touch the pins in the socket', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 66, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00067', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which was the first digital computer to use the von Neumann which used stored programs developed by the two professors who developed ENIAC?', '["IBM 704", "UNIVAC", "EDVAC", "EDSAC", "CDC 3600"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "EDVAC". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 67, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00068', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements is true regarding and CRT monitors?', '["CRT monitors are typically thinner and lighter compared to LCD and LED monitors. LCD LED", "LED monitors use fluorescent backlighting to illuminate the while LCD monitors use light- emitting diodes. LED fudksgr", "LCD and LED monitors consume more power than CRT monitors. LCD LED fudksgr CRT", "LED monitors are type of LCD monitor that use LED backlighting instead of fluorescent backlighting. LED fudksgr", "CRT monitors offer higher resolution and better color accuracy than modern LCD and LED monitors. CRT fudksgr LCD LED"]'::jsonb, 4, 'LCD (Liquid Crystal Display) monitors rely on a liquid crystal layer to control light and create images. Traditional LCD monitors use (Cold Cathode Fluorescent Lamp) backlighting to illuminate the display', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 68, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00069', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What historical event in the 1970s significantly lowered the cost of computers and paved the way for their widespread adoption by individuals and businesses?', '["The invention of the transistor", "The development of the integrated circuit (IC)", "The launch of the first commercial computers by IBM", "The creation of the World Wide Web", "The invention of the mouse"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The development of the integrated circuit (IC) in the 1970s was a transformative event in computer history. IC technology drastically reduced the and power con sumption of electronic devices by integrating multiple transistors and other components onto a single silicon chip', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 69, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00070', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following advancements is most correctly matched to the respective computer generation?', '["First Introduction of assembly language and faster input-output devices", "Second Development of object-oriented programming concepts. fojk", "Third Implementation of time-sharing operating systems and integrated circuits", "Fourth Adoption of vacuum tube-based quantum computing models", "Fifth Emphasis on superconductors as the main computation medium. miajk"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. First-generation computers used vacuum tubes and machine introduced in the second generation. fojk Option 2: Incorrect. Object -oriented programming was conceptualized much during the third and fourth not in the second generation', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 70, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00071', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not a characteristic of a dot matrix printer?', '["Uses an impact printing mechanism", "Produces carbon copies using multipart paper. nyq fldgia lvodis", "Prints by striking an ink ribbon against paper. lvodishg", "Typically has lower printing costs compared to inkjet printers", "Offers near-photographic prints. Wiia"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: Correct. Dot matrix printers strike the paper using tiny pins to form characters. Option 2: Correct. They are often used in invoice printing because of their ability to create multiple copies at once. fndfyda yelshdj ksid Option 3: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 71, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00072', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'The primary access method used for magnetic tape is _____________', '["Sequential", "Random", "Direct", "Manual", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This is the correct method. In magnetic tape data is written and read in a and to retrieve a specific piece of the tape must be wound forward or backward until the correct position is reached', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 72, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00073', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following technologies was used in the second generation of computers?', '["Vacuum Tubes", "Transistors", "Integrated Circuits (ICs)", "Microprocessors", "Artificial Intelligence (AI) Chips"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Used in first generation computers. (1940 - 1956) These were bulky glass tubes that controlled the flow of used as switches in early computers. They produced a lot of were and had frequent failures. Examples Option 2: Used in second generation computers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 73, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00074', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following cannot be true regarding memory devices?', '["V olatile memory loses its data when power is turned off", "ROM is read-only memory and cannot be modified after manufacture. ROM", "SRAM consumes more power compared to DRAM due to its complexity. SRAM", "Cache memory is typically slower than primary memory", "Virtual memory allows the system to use storage as an extension of RAM"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Correct. V olatile memory RAM) requires a continuous power supply to retain data. When the power is all stored data is lost. Option 2: Partially correct. Traditional ROM is read but modern types of ROM like EPROM and EEPROM can be reprogrammed under certain conditions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 74, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00075', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Meera is working on a security system for a high -tech office building. Employees must be able to enter the building quickly and securely without using physical keys. The system should identify each person individually and prevent unauthorized jev blaukska yel s ;ks ;ksj wkjir of the following input devices would be most appropriate for identifying employees in this system?', '["Scanner", "Keyboard", "Game controller", "Webcam", "Biometric fingerprint reader"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: A regular scanner is used for digitizing physical documents or images. It is not used for identifying individuals for security purposes. Option 2: A keyboard allows users to input such as passwords or PINs', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 75, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00076', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following types of printers uses a powder-based ink known as toner?', '["Inkjet printer", "Dot matrix printer", "Thermal printer", "Laser printer", "Plotter"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Inkjet printer uses liquid not toner. The ink is sprayed through tiny nozzles onto the paper. Commonly used for home and office printing. biskq ksjdi Option 2: Dot matrix printer uses an impact mechanism with tiny pins striking an ink ribbon', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 76, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00077', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not a type of optical storage disc?', '["R", "RW", "RE", "ROM", "SSC"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: R (Recordable) is a type of optical disc Data can be written once but not erased. R Option 2: data can be and rewritten multiple times', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 77, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00078', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'The BIOS programme activates as soon as the computer is switched on. The BIOS program is located il%sh jydu BIOS jevigyk', '["Cache Memory", "ROM", "CMOS RAM", "Northbridge Chipset", "Southbridge Chipset"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "ROM". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 78, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00079', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which type of printer uses a toner cartridge and a drum to produce high-quality text and graphics?', '["Inkjet Printer", "Thermal Printer", "Laser Printer", "Dot Matrix Printer", "D Printer"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Laser printers use a laser beam to form an image on a drum. The drum then attracts toner (a fine powder), which is transferred to paper and fused using heat. This process allows for fast printing speeds and high-quality text and especially in professional or office environments', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 79, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00080', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In which generation Monitor used as Input', '["1st Generation", "2nd Generation", "3rd Generation", "4th Generation", "5th Generation"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "3rd Generation". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 80, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00081', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following component is not a part of the standard V on Neumann architecture?', '["Control Unit", "Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)", "Memory Unit", "Input", "Graphics Processing Unit (GPU)"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: It directs the processor''s operations. It fetches instructions from decodes and manages the execution by sending signals to other components. th ilikfha Option 2: Handles all arithmetic and logical operations Option 3: Stores both data and instructions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 81, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00082', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is a type of in which data can only be written once and cannot be erased?', '["PROM", "EPROM", "EEPROM", "RAM", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "PROM". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 82, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00083', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the function of the ALU according to V on Neumann Architecture?', '["Holding small sets of data", "Coordinating various components", "Controls the signals of the computer system", "Decoding the instructions", "Handles the computational tasks"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Von Neumann architecture V on Neumann Architecture is a stored program concept that consists of a memory and input output devices. The program is stored in memory. The CPU fetches an instruction from the memory at a time and executes it. fjdka kshqudka ne.ska ,ndf', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 83, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00084', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which port on the motherboard is commonly used to connect older monitors and projectors?', '["USB", "HDMI", "Display port", "Ethernet", "VGA"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "VGA". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 84, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00085', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements is correct?', '["The Internet marked the beginning of the fourth generation of computers", "Vacuum tubes marked the end of the second generation of computers", "It marked the end of the transistor third generation of computers. g%dkaisiagr", "Operating systems with graphical user interfaces were used in the fourth generation of computers", "The microprocessor marked the beginning of the fifth generation of computers. ilikh miajk"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Incorrect. The fourth generation of computers is typically marked by the development and use of not the Internet. The Internet became widespread much during the development of the World Wide Web in the late 20th century. Option 2: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 85, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00086', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the answer to devices that can be used to directly input bank debit card information?', '["Magnetic strip Flatbed Data loggers", "Magnetic strip NFC Smart card reader", "NFC RFID OCR", "NFC Data OMR", "Magnetic strip RFID"]'::jsonb, 2, 'There are currently 3 methods used to directly input bank credit card information. yr Magnetic strip reader For the magnetic sensitive strip on the card is used. NFC reader This is done by the NFC chip on the card. Smart card reader For a special chip embedded in the card is used', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 86, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00087', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Why is EEPROM preferred over EPROM in modern systems?', '["EEPROM is faster than EPROM", "EEPROM does not require a special erasing process. EEPROM", "EEPROM has unlimited write cycles", "EEPROM is used exclusively for BIOS firmware. EEPROM", "EEPROM consumes more power than EPROM. EPROM"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. EEPROM is slower than EPROM for read operations since it requires extra steps to access data. Option 2: Correct. EPROM requires ultraviolet light to erase which is inconvenient and requires specialized equipment', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 87, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00088', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Time-sharing systems primarily aim', '["Provide long CPU response", "Minimize user tasks", "Reduce CPU idle time", "Support single-user programs", "Handle one process"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is incorrect. Time-sharing systems are designed to provide quick and efficient CPU response not long ones. The goal is to ensure that the CPU time is shared among multiple users or allowing for prompt responses. fnodf', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 88, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00089', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements best describes a Time-Sharing Operating System (TSOS)?', '["It allocates CPU time to multiple users and tasks allowing interactive user experiences. th", "It processes tasks ensuring that each task completes before moving on to the next one", "It focuses solely on batch where jobs are processed in groups without user interaction. th", "It requires dedicated hardware resources for each limiting the number of users. thg", "It utilizes a single-user allowing only one user to access the system at a time. th"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct. It allocates CPU time to multiple users and tasks allowing interactive user experiences', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 89, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00090', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the primary purpose of virtual memory in a computer system?', '["To increase the physical memory capacity by using disk storage", "To improve the speed of data transfer between CPU and RAM CPU RAM", "To provide a backup in case of hardware failure", "To enhance the graphical performance of applications", "To reduce the size of data files stored on disk"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This option is correct. Virtual memory helps extend physical memory by using a portion of the hard allowing the system to run larger applications or more applications than the physical RAM alone can handle. Option 2: This option is incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 90, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00091', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What does the operating system use to run an application that requires more space than the maximum memory space of a computer''s primary memory?', '["Extended memory", "Read only memory", "Virtual memory", "Random Access Memory", "Cache memory"]'::jsonb, 3, '• Virtual Memory Virtual memory is a memory management technique used by operating systems to extend the apparent available memory beyond the physical limits of the computer''s primary memory (RAM). It does this by using a portion of the hard drive or SSD as if it were additional RAM', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 91, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00092', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not a result of hard disk fragmentation?', '["Slows down the hard disk drive", "Longer time to access data", "Some data becomes difficult to access", "Some files in the hard disk can be lost", "Increased Disk Wear and Tear"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Fragmentation causes the hard disk to slow down because the read fragmented files. LKavkh ksid ysi Option 2: Fragmented files result in longer access times since the data is scattered across different parts of disk', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 92, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00093', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements accurately describes a difference between Solid State Drives (SSD) and Hard Disk Drives (HDD)?', '["use magnetic platters to store while use flash memory chips. SSD", "have faster data transfer rates compared to due to their mechanical nature. HDD", "are more resistant to physical shock and vibration than because they lack moving parts", "typically consume less power than making them more energy-efficient. HDD SSD", "have longer average lifespans compared to due to their mechanical durability. SSD"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This statement is incorrect. use flash memory chips to store providing faster access times and better performance', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 93, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00094', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What type of scanner can be used to convert a hard copy into an editable digital copy?', '["OMR", "Flatbed scanner", "OCR", "MICR", "Digitizer"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: OMR scanners are designed to detect marks made on specially designed paper such as checkboxes and bubbles. These scanners are primarily used for grading and questionnaires', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 94, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00095', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not a feature related to simple batch systems?', '["Uniprogramming", "High response time", "Processor sat idle during I", "User directly interacted with the hardware", "OS loaded and executed programs in tape one at a time. tl ne.ska"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Simple Batch Systems Simple batch systems are operating systems that execute a series of jobs in known as without user interaction during processing. This approach increases efficiency by allowing multiple jobs to share resources and reducing idle time for the CPU', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 95, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00096', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not an advantage of virtual memory?', '["Allows a computer to use more memory than what is physically available in RAM. RAM", "Increased Hard Drive", "Manages memory more efficiently", "Prevents Application", "Enables effective multitasking"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Virtual memory extends the usable memory of a computer beyond the physical memory (RAM) by using a portion of the hard drive. This means the system can run more applications or handle larger data than would be possible with RAM alone. Option 2: This is a disadvantage', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 96, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00097', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements about computer generations is MOST ACCURATE?', '["The first generation of computers used transistors and were known for their compact size", "The fourth generation computers relied on vacuum tubes and punch cards for input", "Integrated circuits (ICs) were a defining characteristic of the second generation of computers", "Modern computers with advanced processing power and networking capabilities belong to the first generation. Wiia", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: Incorrect. First generation of computers used vacuum not transistors. Transistors were introduced in the second generation of computers. Option 2: Incorrect. Fourth generation of computers used microprocessors', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 97, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00098', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'The BIOS activates as soon as the computer is switched on. The BIOS programme is located il%sh jydu BIOS jevigyk', '["Cache Memory", "ROM", "CMOS RAM", "Northbridge Chipset", "Southbridge Chipset"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Cache memory is a high -speed volatile memory located close to the designed to speed up access to frequently used data and instructions. It is not used for storing the BIOS', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 98, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00099', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'The main advantage of creating more than one partition in a hard disk is', '["Separation of operating system and program files", "Ability to retrieve files efficiently", "Easiness of making directories and subdirectories", "Easiness of creating multiple users nyq", "Easiness of taking backups of selected files"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This is the most important benefit of partitioning. By separating the operating system (OS) from program files or user you can organize your files more efficiently. If the OS gets you can reinstall it without losing your other data stored on different partitions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 99, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00100', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following data storage devices has the largest capacity?', '["Magnetic Tape", "Floppy Disk", "Solid State Drive", "Pen Drive", "DVD"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Magnetic tapes are renowned for their high storage capacity and making them a favored choice for long -term data storage and archival needs. Their durability ensures data integrity over while sequential access facilitates efficient storage and retrieval processes', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 100, '2027 Quiz Series')
