VALUES
('alict_00101', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the primary difference between dynamic and condenser microphones?', '["The shape and size of the microphone. uhsl%f*dakfha yevh", "The type of sound they capture", "The way they convert sound into an electrical signal", "The length of the microphone cable. uhsl%f*dak", "The type of connector used"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Dynamic Microphones Dynamic microphones use electromagnetic induction to convert sound into an electrical signal. They have a diaphragm attached to a coil of which moves within a magnetic field when sound waves hit generating a current', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 101, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00102', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following has the fastest data access?', '["Virtual memory", "Read only memory", "Cache memory", "Hard disk", "Random access memory"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Cache memory has the fastest data access because it is a high -speed memory located close to the designed to store frequently used data and instructions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 102, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00103', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is an advantage of using a multi-core processor architecture in computer systems?', '["Reduced power consumption", "Increased clock speed", "Improved single-threaded performance", "Enhanced multitasking capability", "Higher bus bandwidth"]'::jsonb, 4, 'A multi-core processor architecture has multiple cores in a single allowing it to perform multiple tasks simultaneously. The primary advantage of using a multi-core processor is enhanced multitasking capability', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 103, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00104', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Cache memory is typically used to store which of the following?', '["To permanently store the most frequently accessed data", "To temporarily store the most frequently accessed data", "To temporarily store large volumes of data", "To permanently store the least frequently accessed data. wju", "To temporarily store the least frequently accessed data. wju"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) To temporarily store the most frequently accessed data. Cache memory is a high-speed memory located close to the CPU and is used to improve processing speed by storing frequently accessed data and instructions. Wmfoia', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 104, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00105', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following best describes the role of the "scheduler" in an operating system?', '["Manages memory allocation for processes", "Decides the order in which processes access the CPU. CPU", "Handles file system operations and storage", "Manages network communication between devices", "Allocates and deallocates resources like printers and scanners"]'::jsonb, 2, 'This is the primary role of the scheduler is deciding the order in which processes access the CPU. kshuldrlfha It uses scheduling algorithms Round Priority Scheduling) to determine which process gets CPU time and in what ensuring efficient CPU utilization and fairness', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 105, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00106', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'The mechanism of allowing multiple tasks to run simultaneously on a single processor is known', '["Multi-threading", "Multiprocessing", "Multitasking", "Multi-allocation", "Multi-sequencing"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is incorrect. Multi-threading refers to the ability of a CPU or a single core in a multi -core processor to execute multiple threads concurrently. it is a subset of multitasking. Multi-threading Option 2: This is incorrect in the context of the question', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 106, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00107', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following storage technologies generally provides the fastest data access speeds for frequently accessed ;dlaIKhkaf.ka imhkafkao@ A. HDD (Hard Disk Drive)', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "B and C only. B C"]'::jsonb, 2, 'SSD (Solid State Drive) use flash which allows for very fast data access speeds. They have no moving resulting in significantly lower latency and faster read SSD wvq m%udohla', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 107, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00108', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Who Invented the first Automatic sequence Calculator (Mark I)?', '["Blaise Pascal", "Charles Babbage", "Howard Aiken", "Alan Turing", "John von Neumann fcdaka fjdka kshqudkaa"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The first automatic sequence known as the Mark was invented by Howard Aiken. He built the Mark I between 1937 and 1945 at Harvard University. The Mark I was a large electromechanical computer that could perform complex calculations automatic ally', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 108, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00109', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In the earliest computers with no operating which of the following was a false statement?', '["Programs were executed one after the other. tlska tl", "Users interacted directly with the hardware", "The processor often sat idle during I", "Batch processing was used to group similar jobs. iudk l%shdjka", "Manual intervention was required for program scheduling"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This statement is true. In early computers without operating programs were executed one at a time in a sequential manner. wdldrfhka Option 2: This statement is true', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 109, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00110', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'A user starts a spreadsheet application on their single processor computer and creates a new spreadsheet. He uses his own database management system and opens database to retrieve certain information needed for spreadsheets. After completing the he saves it. Which of the following features of the operating system has the above user used? (Assume that you have enough RAM for the ;ukaf.a ;ks ilikh lr" kj ,nd Tyq ;ukaf.a ^ lr" iuqodhla Tyq th iqrlshs lr o? RAM tlla context switching', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "A and B only. A B", "A and C only. A C", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A only. A". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 110, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00111', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following devices can function as both input and output?', '["Barcode scanner", "Touchscreen", "Projector", "Printer", "Mouse"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A touchscreen is a versatile device that serves as both an input and output device depending on how it is • As an output the touchscreen displays visual information like any regular monitor or screen. It shows and user interfaces', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 111, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00112', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which component of a computer is responsible for temporarily storing data and instructions that are actively being processed by the CPU?', '["Hard Disk Drive (HDD)", "Random Access Memory (RAM)", "Central Processing Unit (CPU)", "Graphics Processing Unit (GPU)", "Solid State Drive (SSD)"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Hard Disk Drive (HDD) The Hard Disk Drive is used for long-term storage of data and programs. It is a non-volatile storage meaning it retains data even when the computer is turned off. it is not involved in the immediate processing tasks of the CPU', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 112, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00113', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'According to V on Neumann''s the computer is divided into 4 subsystems. What is the selection of those 4 subsystems?', '["firmware", "Input output control unit and memory", "Control Arithmetic and Logic Input Output Unit", "Control Input Output Processing Arithmetic and Logic Unit", "Input Output Processing Circuit"]'::jsonb, 3, 'According to V on Neumann''s the computer is divided into following four main subsystems. V on Neumann f.a • Memory This is where data and instructions are stored', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 113, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00114', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Consider the following ld¾hhka Loading a program from the secondary storage to the main isg m%Odk jevigykla Managing the hard disk Finding the number of characters in a text .Kk fidhd of the above is', '["A only", "B only", "C only", "A and B only", "All of the above. A B C A B"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Statement This is indeed a core function of an operating system. The OS manages the process of loading programs into main memory (RAM) from secondary storage (like a hard disk) so that they can be executed. This function is essential for program execution and memory management', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 114, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00115', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements best describes the difference between primary and secondary storage in a computer system?', '["Primary storage is used for long -term data while secondary storage is used for temporary data storage and is faster", "Primary storage includes devices like hard drives and while secondary storage includes volatile memory such as RAM", "Primary storage is faster and used for immediate data whereas secondary storage is slower and used for long-term data storage", "Primary storage is used exclusively for storing operating system while secondary storage is used for user data only", "Primary storage refers to external devices connected to the while secondary storage refers to internal components"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Primary storage (such as RAM) is faster and used for immediate access to data that is currently being processed by the computer. It is meaning the data is lost when the power is turned off', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 115, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00116', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is incorrect regarding a process?', '["A single program can have many processes", "A single process can have many programs", "A process can be executed by the CPU", "A process is not a program", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: True. A program is a set of and multiple instances of the same program can run as separate processes. For you can open multiple instances of a text each of which is a separate process. jevigykla Option 2: False', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 116, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00117', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What does RPM stand for in the context of hard disk drives', '["Reads per minute", "Revolutions per month", "Rotations per minute", "Randomized platter movement", "Revamped platter mechanism"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Rotations per minute". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 117, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00118', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements correctly describes the difference between SRAM and DRAM?', '["SRAM is more and has higher storage density than SRAM", "DRAM is volatile and cost per bit is lower. DRAM", "DRAM is less expensive and has less storage density than SRAM. DRAM", "SRAM requires refreshing to maintain while DRAM does not. SRAM", "DRAM is used primarily for CPU cache memory due to high speed DRAM"]'::jsonb, 2, 'SRAM is used for applications where speed is critical and the amount of memory needed is relatively such as CPU caches. It is more expensive per bit and offers lower storage density', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 118, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00119', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following uses sequential access?', '["RAM", "Magnetic tape", "Hard disk", "CD", "ROM"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Sequential access Sequential access requires data to be accessed in a ordered sequence. To reach a particular piece of all preceding data may need to be processed first. Random access Random access allows data to be read from or written to any location directly and immediately', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 119, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00120', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of these is the technology used in Blue-Ray discs?', '["Semi-conductor Technology", "Solid State Technology", "Optical Media Technology", "Magnetic Media Technology", "Electro-magnetic Technology"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Semi-conductor Technology This is used in the manufacturing of electronic components like and integrated but not specifically for data storage on discs', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 120, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00121', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the maximum number of processes that can be in the running state simultaneously on a single- core processor?', '["0", "1", "2", "3", "Unlimited"]'::jsonb, 2, 'On a single-core only one process can be in the running state at any given time. The CPU can only execute one instruction at a time', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 121, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00122', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following printers spray tiny droplets of ink onto paper to produce images and text?', '["Dot matrix printer", "Laser printer", "Line printer", "Thermal printer", "Inkjet printer"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Dot Matrix Printer This type of printer creates images and text by striking an ink ribbon with a matrix of tiny producing dots on the paper. It doesn''t use ink droplets. myr 2', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 122, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00123', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the purpose of the suspended state in process management?', '["Indicating that a process is currently executing on the CPU. CPU", "Moving a process from main memory to secondary memory. m%Odk", "Creating a new process", "Terminating a running process", "Moving a process from the waiting state to the ready state"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Let''s consider each option one by one. Option 1: According to this it''s false. The suspended state does not indicate that a process is executing on the th fkdfmkajhs thska Option 2: According to this it''s true', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 123, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00124', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the main purpose of parallel and grid computing?', '["Enhancing CPU compatibility", "Reducing hardware costs", "Increasing computational power by distributing tasks", "Improving storage device performance", "Simplifying hardware interfaces"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Parallel Computing Involves dividing a task into smaller subtasks and processing them simultaneously using multiple processors. This increases computational power and efficiency', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 124, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00125', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not a characteristic of a process when compared to processes and programs?', '["Programs that are currently active", "Stored in RAM", "Destroyed after execution", "Stored on the hard disk", "Is dynamic"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This is characteristic of operations. Active programs (or processes) are running and performing tasks. bgq Option 2: Operations or processes that are currently running are stored in RAM (Random Access Memory), which is faster and volatile', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 125, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00126', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which emerging input device technology utilizes hand gestures and movements to interact with computers without physical contact?', '["Voice recognition", "Brain computer interface (BCI)", "Eye tracking", "Machine learning", "D scanner"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Brain-computer interface (BCI) technology allows users to control computer systems or devices using brain typically detected through electroencephalography (EEG) sensors', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 126, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00127', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following best describes the correct sequence of operations in the Fetch-Execute Cycle of a CPU?', '["Execute \u2192 Decode \u2192 Fetch", "Fetch \u2192 Execute \u2192 Decode", "Decode \u2192 Fetch \u2192 Execute", "Fetch \u2192 Decode \u2192 Execute", "Decode \u2192 Execute \u2192 Fetch"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Fetch The CPU starts by fetching (retrieving) the instruction from the memory. This is the first step because the processor needs to know what operation to perform. CPU tl Decode After fetching the CPU decodes it to understand what actions are required', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 127, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00128', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is an example of volatile memory?', '["Hard Disk", "ROM", "RAM", "PROM", "EEPROM"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Random Access Memory (RAM) is a type of volatile memory because it only holds data while the computer is powered on. Once the power is turned the data in RAM is lost. Why the other options are not suitable Option 1: This is a non-volatile memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 128, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00129', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the main role of the long-term scheduler?', '["To control the degree of multiprogramming", "To allocate CPU time to processes", "To handle process synchronization", "To manage paging in memory", "To resolve deadlocks"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The long-term also known as the job is responsible for deciding which processes are admitted into the system for processing. Its primary role is to control the degree of multiprogramming by admitting programs from job pool and loading them into the main memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 129, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00130', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which port is commonly used for connecting high-definition displays and supports both audio and video signals?', '["USB-C", "DVI", "DisplayPort", "PS", "Serial port"]'::jsonb, 3, 'USB-C According to this it is false. USB-C is versatile and supports both data transfer and video signals. it is not specifically designed for high-definition displays', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 130, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00131', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In which device is sequential access used to access data in computers?', '["RAM (Random access memory)", "Hard disk", "Magnetic tape", "SSD (solid-state drive)", "CD (Compact Disc)"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Sequential access In this method data is accessed only from one passing other data till we find the data that we are looking for. Sequential access is used in magnetic tapes', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 131, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00132', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the primary purpose of a file system in an operating system?', '["To manage the CPU scheduling", "To provide a mechanism for file storage and retrieval", "To handle network communication", "To manage hardware devices", "None above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is the role of the CPU not the file system. CPU Option 2: This is the core function of a file allowing users to and organize files on storage devices. ,nd', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 132, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00133', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'In a modern gaming which of the following components commonly employs CMOS technology for temporary data storage that is crucial for real-time rendering and gameplay?', '["The Blu-ray disc drive", "The internal hard disk drive or solid-state drive", "The power supply unit", "The main graphics processing unit''s (GPU) dedicated memory. m%Odk .%e*sla", "The network interface card"]'::jsonb, 4, 'CMOS (Complementary Metal-Oxide-Semiconductor) technology is widely used in memory chips due to its low power consumption and high integration density. This makes it ideal for creating large and fast memory modules', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 133, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00134', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following does not support the booting process of a computer?', '["System software", "Application software", "Hardware", "Liveware", "Firmware"]'::jsonb, 2, 'System Software During the booting the system software is responsible for initializing hardware loading necessary device and starting essential system services. It plays a crucial role in bootstrapping the computer into a functional state', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 134, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00135', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What happens when the current program in a Simple Batch System completes execution?', '["The system shuts down and waits for jid oud", "The OS switches to a new user interface", "The OS loads the next program from the queue automatically", "The results are permanently deleted from memory", "The processor enters idle mode. ilikh"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In a Simple Batch the operating system is designed to execute jobs sequentially without user intervention', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 135, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00136', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is correct about CPU ? CPU o? A. Southbridge chipset helps to carry signals among the main devices. Southbridge m%Odk ix{d', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Statement Incorrect. In the traditional Northbridge -Southbridge the Southbridge manages communication with slower peripheral and input high-speed components such as RAM is handled by the Northbridge. Statement Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 136, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00137', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements best describes the role of a Memory Management Unit (MMU) in memory mapping and its significance in modern computer systems?', '["The MMU maps logical addresses directly to disk addresses to enhance data retrieval speed", "The MMU translates virtual addresses to physical addresses and manages memory and paging. MMU u.ska", "The MMU directly increases the size of physical memory by compressing data in RAM. MMU RAM", "The MMU only handles cache memory management to reduce CPU access time frequently used data. MMU", "The MMU bypasses the need for virtual memory by ensuring that all processes fit into the physical memory available. MMU"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct statement that best describes the role of a Memory Management Unit (MMU) in memory mapping and its significance in modern computer systems is 2) The MMU translates virtual addresses to physical addresses and manages memory and paging', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 137, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00138', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Manitha powers on his computer and opens a then a video and later a text editor. Which of the following are possible execution sequences on the processor of his computer?', '["BIOS \u2192 OS \u2192 browser process \u2192 OS \u2192 video player process \u2192 OS \u2192 text editor process \u2192 OS \u2192", "BIOS \u2192 browser process \u2192 OS \u2192 video player process \u2192 OS \u2192 text editor process \u2192 OS \u2192", "BIOS \u2192 OS \u2192 video player process \u2192 browser process \u2192 OS \u2192 text editor process \u2192 OS \u2192", "BIOS \u2192 OS \u2192 browser process \u2192 video player process \u2192 text editor process \u2192 OS \u2192 browser process \u2192", "BIOS \u2192 OS \u2192 video player process \u2192 text editor process \u2192 browser process \u2192 OS \u2192 video player process \u2192"]'::jsonb, 1, 'To determine the correct execution sequence of processes on a computer''s let''s analyze the provided options and how a computer''s boot and task execution process works. ilikhl • BIOS (Basic Input This is the first software that runs when the computer is powered on', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 138, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00139', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the main purpose of a preemptive scheduler in an operating system?', '["It allows a process to run until it voluntarily releases the CPU. th CPU uqod", "It ensures that a process completes execution before switching to another process. th", "It allows the operating system to interrupt a running process and assign the CPU to another process. th", "It prevents context switching between processes. th", "It only schedules processes in a First-Served manner. th"]'::jsonb, 3, 'It allows a process to run until it voluntarily releases the CPU. - Incorrect th CPU uqod This describes non-preemptive where the CPU is only reassigned when a process completes or voluntarily yields control', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 139, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00140', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not a key characteristic of Von Neumann architecture?', '["Use of a single memory for both instructions and data. Wmfoia", "Sequential execution of instructions", "Parallel processing capabilities at the hardware level", "Use of a central processing unit (CPU)", "Instructions are fetched from memory and executed by the CPU Wmfoia"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Von Neumann architecture features a single memory for instructions and data and follows sequential execution. fjdka kshqudka wkq.ukh Explanation of each option 1: Single memory is a characteristic of Von Neumann architecture', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 140, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00141', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following mechanisms allows a graphical user interface (GUI) to manage resource-intensive operations without interrupting user interactions?', '["Kernel preemption", "Lazy evaluation in the processor", "Multithreading in window management", "Single-threaded execution of system calls", "Static resource allocation in memory"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is Incorrect. Kernel preemption allows the operating system to interrupt a running process in kernel mode to ensure high-priority tasks are executed. While it improves system it is not directly tied to GUI-specific operations like managing resource-intensive tasks', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 141, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00142', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'While Tharindu was printing a multi-page suddenly the printer ran out of paper. Tharindu immediately re-inserts the paper and resumes the printing process. According to the seven-state process transition which of the following best describes the above scenario?', '["The printing process enters the blocked state and then it enters the ready and running respectively", "The printing process enters the swapped and blocked state and then terminates", "The printing process goes into the swapped and waiting states and then into the ready and", "The print operation terminates and starts again from the created state", "The printing process goes into the blocked state and returns to the created state and starts"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct. When the printer runs out of the printing process moves to the blocked state as it cannot continue. Once the paper is the process transitions to the ready state and eventually back to the running state to continue printing', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 142, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00143', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Consider the following statements about Contiguous Allocation. hdno Contiguously allocated files can be used efficiently afterwards. hdno ,o miqj yel'' B. It is efficient to find the space compatible with the size of the file in hard disk to save the file. f.dkqj iq', '["A Only A", "C Only C", "A and B Only A B", "A and C Only A C", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Statement This Statement is True. Contiguous allocation places all the data of a file in a continuous block of making it highly efficient for sequential access. The system can read or write the data quickly since there''s no need to jump between memory locations', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 143, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00144', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is meant by firmware?', '["Software that controls hardware devices", "A type of hardware component in computers. ixrpl", "Temporary memory used for storing data", "Physical circuitry responsible for processing instructions. Wmfoia", "A type of programming language commonly used in embedded systems"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Software that controls hardware devices". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 144, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00145', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is a hardware mechanism that maps virtual addresses to physical addresses?', '["Control unit", "Bus", "Arithmetic and logic unit", "Cache memory", "Memory management unit"]'::jsonb, 5, 'The Memory Management Unit (MMU) is a hardware component in a computer system that translates virtual addresses (used by programs) into physical addresses (used by RAM). It enables virtual memory functionality by managing address memory and paging mechanisms', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 145, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00146', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'During a process references a virtual memory address. The page table entry for that th ,smskhla fhduq tu olajd The page is valid in the virtual address space', '["When the CPU detects that the referenced page is not currently loaded in physical memory fhduq ,o oekg", "When the operating system decides to replace a page in memory using a page replacement algorithm", "When the page table entry is accessed regardless of the present bit value", "When the process terminates before completing memory access", "When the disk interrupt signals completion of page loading"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Given • The page is valid in the virtual address space. • The present • The page has been swapped to disk. tu oekg This means The page logically belongs to the process.But it is not currently in physical memory (RAM)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 146, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00147', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which generation of computers is mainly associated with the development of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and expert systems?', '["First Generation", "Second Generation", "Third Generation", "Fourth Generation", "Fifth Generation"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "Fifth Generation". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 147, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00148', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statements best describes the primary difference between a digitizer and a graphics tablet?', '["A digitizer is typically used for converting drawings into digital whereas a graphics tablet is used for creating digital art directly on the computer. digitizer", "A graphics tablet requires a stylus for while a digitizer can only be used with a mouse. .%e*sla", "A digitizer provides a touch-sensitive while a graphics tablet uses light sensors to detect input. digitizer", "A graphics tablet can only be used with specific while a digitizer is compatible with any drawing software. .%e*sla", "A digitizer can create 3D whereas a graphics tablet is limited to 2D drawings. digitizer"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A digitizer is typically used for converting drawings into digital whereas a graphics tablet is used for creating digital art directly on the computer. digitizer". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 148, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00149', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not an information commonly found in the Process Control Block (PCB) of the Operating System ?', '["Process number", "Capacity of hard disk", "Process scheduling state", "Program counter", "Process state"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The Process Control Block (PCB) is a data structure in the operating system that stores important information about a process. The PCB typically contains the following 1. Process A unique identifier assigned to each process. 2', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 149, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00150', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which operating system component is responsible for scheduling CPU time for the process and preventing it from exceeding its allocated execution time?', '["The process scheduler", "The memory manager", "The interrupt handler", "The file system manager", "The device manager"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct. Manages process execution and enforces time terminating processes that exceed their allocated time. Option 2: Incorrect. Handles memory allocation and unrelated to time limits. Option 3: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 2027, 150, '2027 Quiz Series')
