VALUES
('alict_00301', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What is the primary advantage of using universal gates (NAND or NOR) in digital circuit design?', '["They simplify circuit diagrams by reducing the number of gates needed. oajdr .Kk wvq igyka", "They are easier to build in integrated circuits", "They have the fastest switching speed among all gates. oajdr", "They consume the least amount of power in all operations", "They eliminate the need for flip-flops in sequential circuits"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The primary advantage of using universal such as NAND and in digital circuit design is that they are easier to build in integrated as stated in Option 2. NAND and NOR gates are considered universal because any other logical gate etc', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 301, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00302', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Given the Boolean expression (A⨁B) + C. and if inputs A = 0 and B = 0, what are the possible outputs based on different values of C?', '["A only", "B only", "C only", "A and B only", "A and C only A B C A B A C"]'::jsonb, 2, 'By building a truth table for all possible values of and we can easily determine the outputs corresponding to different instances. B C ICN A B C A⨁B C. A (A⨁B) + C', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 302, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00303', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'In an SR latch made with NOR what is the result when both S (Set) and R (Reset) inputs are HIGH simultaneously?', '["The latch sets the output to 1", "The latch resets the output to 0", "The latch toggles its output", "The latch enters an invalid or undefined state. latch tl", "The output remains in its previous state"]'::jsonb, 4, 'When both S and R are HIGH (1) The output Q and Q̅ both go LOW (0) because the NOR gates see at least one HIGH input. NOR oajdr wju HIGH wdodkhla olsk ksid" This violates the fundamental requirement that Q and Q̅ should always be complementary when one is 1, the other is 0)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 303, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00304', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Consider a logic gate with three inputs and the output follows this truth C oajdrhla wkq.ukh lrhs( Which of the following Boolean expressions best represents the output Q?', '["A \u0305 + AB \u0305", "A \u0305 B + A \u0305 B \u0305 + AB \u0305", "A \u0305 + B \u0305", "A \u0305 B \u0305", "A\u0305"]'::jsonb, 3, 'We can use both Karnaugh Map (K -map) and Boolean expression simplification methods to solve this question. Let''s solve this question using each method', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 304, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00305', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following correctly matches a computing generation with its major technology?', '["First Generation - Transistors", "Second Generation - Vacuum Tubes", "Third Generation - Integrated Circuits", "Fourth Generation - Mechanical Gears", "Fifth Generation - Punch Cards"]'::jsonb, 3, 'First Generation Incorrect. The first generation of computers (1951 -1958) used vacuum not transistors. These machines were and generated a lot of heat. 2) Second Generation Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 305, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00306', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is a unique characteristic of plotters that distinguishes them from traditional printers?', '["Plotters are faster at producing detailed text-based documents", "Plotters use vector graphics to create continuous lines rather than rasterized dots", "Plotters are optimized for producing 3D models and simulations", "Plotters are primarily used for compact document printing in offices. m%Odk", "Plotters can only print using monochrome ink"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Plotters are not designed for text-heavy documents and are generally slower compared to traditional printers. text-heavy Option 2: Correct. Plotters use vector which rely on mathematical equations to draw continuous lines', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 306, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00307', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the basic principle behind offset printing?', '["Directly transferring ink from a plate to the paper", "Using heat to transfer toner from a drum to the paper isg lvodish", "Spraying ink onto the paper through nozzles", "Transferring ink from a plate to a rubber blanket and then to the paper", "Using static electricity to attract ink to the paper lvodish"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Transferring ink from a plate to a rubber blanket and then to the paper".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 307, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00308', 12, 'General ICT', 'Who made programs of the UNIV AC (Universal Automatic Calculator) to do 10000 calculations per second?', '["Grace Hopper", "John Presper Eckert", "John William Mauchly", "William Shockley", "Walter Brattain"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Grace Hopper".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 308, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00309', 12, 'General ICT', '2108 + 11011012 = ................ What is the correct answer to the triviality given above?', '["111001012", "110101102", "111101012", "1001111112", "101111102"]'::jsonb, 3, 'the octal number here must be converted to binary. 2108 = ....................2 1 0 22 21 20 22 21 20 22 21 20 4 2 1 4 2 1 4 2 1 0 1 0 1 0 2108 = 100010002 the answer must be obtained by adding the two binary numbers together', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 309, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00310', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements best highlights a social benefit of ICT in daily life?', '["ICT makes it possible to create and distribute software legally without licenses", "ICT can increase productivity in manufacturing but reduces employment in other u.ska yels", "ICT improves access to enabling people to connect and collaborate globally", "ICT reduces the environmental impact of electronic waste through continuous upgrades", "ICT allows users to access high-quality reducing the need for physical activities"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is a legal or economic not primarily social. Option 2: This relates more to economic impacts rather than social benefits. iudc Option 3: Correct. This highlights ICT''s role in fostering global social connections and collaboration', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 310, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00311', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statement(s) about off-the-shelf software is', '["Off-the-shelf software is ready-made and available for immediate use", "The software is designed for general purposes and may not fully meet specific organizational needs", "Off-the-shelf software may require some training but generally has user -friendly interfaces designed for a broad audience", "It requires a long development and implementation time. th", "It is usually cost-effective because development costs are spread across many users"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "It requires a long development and implementation time. th".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 311, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00312', 12, 'General ICT', 'If A2+B10 = 111012, which of the following can be A and B respectively?', '["11001, 4", "11000, 4", "11001, 5", "4, 11001", "5, 11001"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "11001, 4".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 312, '2027 Quiz Series'),
