('alict_00375', 12, 'General ICT', 'Who invented the world''s first electronic digital computer?', '["Charles Babbage", "John Vincent Atanasoff & Clifford Berry", "John V on Neumann", "Herman Hollerith", "Joseph Jacquard"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The Atanasoff-Berry Computer (ABC) was the world''s first electronic digital developed between 1937 and 1942 by John Vincent Atanasoff and his graduate student Clifford Berry at Iowa State College (now Iowa State University). (ABC) 1937 1942 wegkdfid*a', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 375, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00376', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following inventions does not belong to the electromechanical kj fkdjkafka Tabulating Machine', '["A and C only. A C", "A and B only. A B", "B and C only. B C", "All of the above", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A. Tabulating Machine - Electromechanical Era The tabulating invented by Herman Hollerith in 1890, was an electromechanical device designed to process punched cards for census data analysis', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 376, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00377', 12, 'General ICT', 'A security system uses three Motion (M), Door (D), and Window (W). An alarm (A) is triggered if either the Door or Window is but only if there is no motion detected. Which combination of logic gates correctly represents the alarm condition?', '["A = (M AND D) OR (M AND W)", "A = M AND (D OR W)", "A = (NOT M) AND (D OR W)", "A = (NOT M) OR (D AND W)", "A = (M OR D) AND (M OR W)"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In this security the alarm (A) is triggered if either the Door (D) or Window (W) is but only if there is no motion detected (NOT M). This can be broken down into two conditions • The Door (D) or Window (W) is breached (logical OR operation between D and W)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 377, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00378', 12, 'General ICT', 'Calculate the answer for 3A16 + 568. 3A16 + 568', '["1101002", "A16", "10410", "10210", "1498"]'::jsonb, 3, 'we should convert the above given numbers into decimal. 3A16 3 A (10) 161 160 3 × 16 10 × 1 48 + 10 5810 we can add the two decimal numbers and get the result easily. 5810 + 4610 = 10410', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 378, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00379', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the largest among the followings?', '["1101002", "1000012", "80", "268", "E16"]'::jsonb, 5, 'First we have to convert all the given number into decimals so that it is easy to select the biggest number because all numbers are in the same base of 10', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 379, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00380', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is a social benefit provided by ICT?', '["Increase in GDP", "Growth in trade statistics", "Enhanced productivity in manufacturing. ksIamdokfha", "New ways for people to interact and like chatting", "Reduced access to the internet"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "New ways for people to interact and like chatting".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 380, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00381', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is a direct impact of ICT on productivity ?', '["Reduced labor productivity. wvq Y%u", "No effect on economic productivity", "Decrease in manufacturing productivity", "Increased productivity in various including manufacturing", "Limited productivity growth in ICT. ICT"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Increased productivity in various including manufacturing".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 381, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00382', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements is false regarding computer screens?', '["LED and LCD screens are also known as Flat-panel displays. LED LCD", "Images of CRT screens are produced using an electron beam. CRT", "Transistors are utilized in screens of CRT monitors. CRT", "LED monitors generate low heat compared to CRT monitors. LED", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Correct. LED and LCD screens are categorized as flat-panel displays because they are thin and unlike bulky CRT monitors. Option 2: Correct. CRT monitors use an electron beam those scans across a phosphor-coated screen to create images', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 382, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00383', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is a direct benefit of ICT in supply chain management?', '["Increased paperwork", "Real-time tracking and inventory management", "Decreased coordination across locations", "Reduced digital communication", "Limited logistics options"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Real-time tracking and inventory management".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 383, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00384', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements is TRUE regarding e-waste and ICT?', '["E-waste does not have any significant impact on the environment", "Safe disposal of e-waste is a key aspect of environmental responsibility in ICT", "ICT advancements have eliminated the issue of e-waste. ICT ksid", "E-waste refers only to waste generated by outdated software", "Recycling is not a viable option for managing e-waste from ICT. ICT"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Safe disposal of e-waste is a key aspect of environmental responsibility in ICT".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 384, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00385', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the answer of the following equation?', '["123410", "139510", "174710", "221310", "163210"]'::jsonb, 2, 'let''s convert the non-decimal numbers to decimal. 5178 5 1 7 82 81 80 5 × 64 1 × 8 7 × 1 320 + 8 + 7 33510 43D16 4 3 D (13) 162 161 160 4 × 256 3 × 16 13 × 1 1024 + 48 + 13 108510 2025/03/11 Information and Communication Technology let''s do the calculation. miqj" wms', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 385, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00386', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following are ethical or legal concerns in ICT?', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "A and C only. A C", "B and C only. B C", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "A and C only. A C".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 386, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00387', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements is true regarding inkjet and laser printers?', '["Inkjet printers use toner cartridges to print whereas laser printers use liquid ink cartridges", "Laser printers are typically slower than inkjet printers when printing large volumes of documents", "Inkjet printers are generally better for high-quality photo printing compared to laser printers", "Laser printers are less expensive to maintain and operate over time compared to inkjet printers", "Both inkjet and laser printers require regular calibration to maintain print quality"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Inkjet printers are well-suited for printing high-quality photos because they use liquid which can produce a wide range of vibrant colors and finer details. This makes them the preferred choice for tasks requiring precise color such as printing photographs or graphics', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 387, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00388', 12, 'General ICT', 'Consider the following 10112 = 1310 = D16 Which of the following is true?', '["Only A is correct", "Only B is correct", "Both A and B are correct", "Both A and B are incorrect", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'let''s convert 10112 into decimal and 1310 into hexadecimal. 10112 1 0 1 23 22 21 20 8 0 2 1 1110 16 13 0 - 13 (D) So 10112 = 1110 1310 = D16S', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 388, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00389', 12, 'General ICT', 'What characteristic distinguishes application software from system software?', '["It includes programs that manage hardware resources directly", "It is primarily designed to solve specific user requirements or needs. th", "It is mandatory for the functioning of a computer system", "It cannot be purchased as a standalone product. th", "It operates only on proprietary software environments. th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Application software is created to perform specific tasks that meet the needs of users. Examples include word web bro and gaming applications', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 389, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00390', 12, 'General ICT', 'In signed-magnitude which bit is used to represent the sign of a number?', '["The least significant bit", "The second most significant bit", "The middle bit", "Last bits", "The most significant bit"]'::jsonb, 5, 'In signed -magnitude the most significant bit (MSB) is used to represent the sign of a number. (MSB) Least significant bit While some representations use the LSB for the signed-magnitude doesn''t', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 390, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00391', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following computer screens has the highest color reproduction? j¾K ;srfhao@ A. CRT screen', '["A Only", "C Only", "A and B Only", "B and C Only", "B and C all"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A Only".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 391, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00392', 12, 'General ICT', 'The answer obtained by calculating 110011012 + 568 - 2716 is equal 110011012 + 568 - 2716 hk .Kkh ,efnk', '["110010102", "110101012", "110101002", "110111002", "100111002"]'::jsonb, 3, 'To perform the three values must be added. since they are in different let''s convert all the values to binary. The addition can then be carried out in binary', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 392, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00393', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the perimeter of the shape below?', '["528", "4210", "C16", "1018", "8216"]'::jsonb, 3, 'To find the perimeter of the given we need to add all the sides together. Step Add the octal values The perimeter of the shape is 54₈. Since none of the options match 54₈, let''s convert this into decimal and hexadecimal', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 393, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00394', 12, 'General ICT', '9710 + 7E16 - 010100112 =', '["8310", "12610", "23310", "14010", "14110"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Converting hexadecimal to decimal 7 E 161 160 7 × 16 14 × 1 112 14 112 + 14 12610 Converting binary to decimal 0 1 0 1 0 1 27 26 25 24 23 22 21 20 0×128 1×64 0×32 1×16 0×8 0×4 1×2 1×1 16 - - 2 1 64 + 16 + 2 + 1 8310', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 394, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00395', 12, 'General ICT', 'Choose the correct statement', '["A = B = C", "A = C", "A = B", "B", "A"]'::jsonb, 2, 'let''s convert B and C into decimal 1448 6316 1 4 6 3 82 81 80 161 160 1 × 64 4 × 8 4 × 1 6 × 16 3 × 1 64 32 4 96 3 64 + 32 + 4 96 + 3 10010 9910 11001002 0 1 0 1 0 27 26 25 24 23 22 21 20 128 × 0 64 × 1 32 × 1 16 × 0 8 × 0 4 × 1 2 × 0 1 × 0 - 64 32 - - 64 + 32 + 4 10010', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 395, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00396', 12, 'General ICT', 'EF16 - 8410 = ............?', '["3578", "1248", "111011002", "B16", "24010"]'::jsonb, 4, 'To solve this first we need to convert the above values to a same base. .Kkh Conversion of hexadecimal to decimal EF16 E (14) F (15) 161 160 16 × 14 1 × 15 224 + 15 23910 = 23910 - 8410 = 15510 let''s convert 15510 to different bases to find the correct answer', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 396, '2027 Quiz Series'),
