('alict_00463', 12, 'General ICT', 'In the IEEE single-precision floating-point what does the exponent field represent?', '["The sign of the mantissa", "The fractional part of the number", "The power of 2 by which the mantissa is multiplied", "The total number of bits used to represent the number", "The number of significant digits in the number"]'::jsonb, 3, 'This standard represents floating-point numbers using 32 bits is divided into three Information and Communication Technology 2026/07/24 • Sign bit Indicates whether the number is positive or negative. • Exponent field Stores the which determines the magnitude of the number', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 463, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00464', 12, 'General ICT', '(AN + D ̅ ) AND (A(AN)D ̅ ) What is the answer when the above expression is trivial?', '["AND\u0305", "AND", "1", "AN + D\u0305", "D\u0305"]'::jsonb, 1, '= (AN + D̅) AND (A(AN)D̅) = (AN + D̅) AND (AAND̅) Distributive law = (AN + D ̅ ) AND (AND ̅ ) Idempotent law = (AN + D̅) . AND̅ AND = " . " = AN. AND̅ + D̅. AND̅ Distributive law = AND̅ + D̅', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 464, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00465', 12, 'General ICT', 'Below are three statements about memory management. Identify which of the following options correctly describes their truth value', '["Only A is true", "Only A and B are true", "Only B is true", "Only B and C are true", "All statements are true"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Statement False. Swapping does not depend on the absence of a memory hierarchy. Swapping is a mechanism where processes are moved between main memory and secondary and it can occur in systems with or without a memory hierarchy. Statement True', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 465, '2027 Quiz Series'),
