('alict_00474', 12, 'General ICT', 'A Global Aerospace Research Organization conducts two computational u.ska folla ,nhs( Program X : Real-time aerodynamic turbulence simulation for spacecraft re -entry. The system requires tightly coupled continuous shared memory and ultra -low latency communication within a single supercomputing facility. wNHjldY tightly coupled ;ks myiqlula wvq mudjla Processing satellite image datasets collected from multiple where each dataset can be analyzed independently across research centers operating under different administrative domains. jevigyk iuqodhka architectural decision is most theoretically and practically justified?', '["Deploy grid computing for both programs to ensure scalability", "Deploy parallel computing for Program X and grid computing for Program Y . jevigyk X", "Deploy grid computing for Program X because it provides better fault tolerance", "Deploy parallel computing for both programs due to higher computational speed", "Deploy grid computing for Program Y only if latency requirements are below microsecond level. mudj uhsfl%da"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct architecture can be identified by considering how closely the processing tasks must work together and where the computing resources are located', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 474, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00475', 12, 'General ICT', 'What is the primary role of the Control Unit during the Fetch-Execute Cycle?', '["Perform arithmetic and logical operations", "Store the results of executed instructions", "Fetch instructions from memory and decode them", "Delete instructions after execution", "Manage input"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The Control Unit (CU) is responsible for managing the Fetch-Execute Cycle. Its primary tasks • Fetching the next instruction from memory • Decoding the instructions to understand what operation to perform. • Coordinating the execution by sending control signals to other CPU components', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 475, '2027 Quiz Series'),
