('alict_00497', 12, 'General ICT', 'NOT operation of the value 1100012 will 1100012 w.fha NOT fufyhqu', '["1110102", "0101012", "0001102", "11110102", "0011102"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Explanation of the NOT Operation on Binary Numbers The NOT also known as bitwise NOT or binary is a fundamental operation in binary logic. This operation works by inverting each bit of a binary number. In other each 1 in the binary number becomes a 0, and each 0 becomes a 1', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 497, '2027 Quiz Series'),
